course: dictionary
lesson: 3908
title: Frills, from dresses to lizards
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one is meant. A frill is a strip of folded cloth on a dress or curtain. Look at the words around it: «The little girl twirled in her dress with a pink frill at the hem.» Dress and twirled are the clues.
explain: The same word can name a part of an animal. «The Australian frilled lizard opens a huge neck frill and hisses to startle predators.» Opens, huge, hisses and predators tell you the frill is a ruffle-like part on the lizard's neck, and that the lizard spreads it out to look bigger and scarier.
explain: Sometimes frill means extra things that are nice but not needed. «No-frills» means simple and cheap, as in a no-frills airline. Ask: what word would fit here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A frill is a strip of cloth with lots of folds, sewn on the edge of a dress, curtain or collar for decoration.
fact: A frill can also be a ruffle-like part on an animal, such as the frill around the neck of a frilled lizard.
fact: The frilled lizard spreads its neck frill to scare enemies away.
fact: «No frills» means simple and cheap, as in a no-frills airline.
fact: «Frilly» dresses show old-fashioned or fancy clothes.
exercise: «The little girl twirled in her dress, which had a pink frill round the hem.» What is a frill here? | A simple, cheap flight | A bony part on a dinosaur's head | A kind of lizard | *A strip of folded cloth sewn on for decoration
exercise: «The frilled lizard opens a huge neck frill and hisses to startle predators.» Why does it open its frill? | To swim faster | *To scare enemies away | To sing to its friends | To keep warm in the sun
exercise: «The no-frills airline has no free food and no fancy seats.» What does no-frills mean? | Free for everyone | *Simple and cheap | Very fancy and expensive | Full of folds and lace
test: «Triceratops had three horns and a huge bony frill.» What kind of frill does Triceratops have? | A strip of cloth on a collar | A pink ribbon for its dress | A simple, cheap ticket | *A huge bony part on its head
test: Mia says frilly dresses are plain and boring. What is wrong with her idea? | Frilly means the same as cheap | Frilly means hungry | *Frilly dresses are fancy, with ruffles, not plain | Frilly means a grey, wet day
exam: «The axolotl keeps its feathery frills on its head all its life.» Which meaning of frill fits best here? | A simple, cheap airline | *A ruffle-like part on an animal | A strip of folded cloth on a dress | Extra things that are nice but not needed
